            <ArticleTitle>Modular Access to Triarylethylene Units from Arylvinyl MIDA Boronates Using a Regioselective Heck Coupling.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>5046-5049</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1021/acs.orglett.7b02218</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A palladium-catalyzed, silver-mediated Heck coupling between arylvinyl MIDA boronate esters and aryl iodides is disclosed. The reaction provides an efficient and modular access to a range of 1,1-diaryl alkenyl MIDA boronates that can be easily transformed into triarylethylene compounds through a Suzuki coupling.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
